  "goodToKnow": "Der Kranz is a wreath: einen Kranz niederlegen (to lay a wreath, at memorials or funerals), der Lorbeerkranz (laurel wreath). The Adventskranz, with four candles lit one by one on the Sundays before Christmas, was invented in Hamburg in 1839 by Johann Hinrich Wichern. Der Frankfurter Kranz is a ring cake with buttercream and brittle. Plural: die Kränze."
